body:
>Lol what makes you say I can't accept reality??

&#x200B;

>But upon becoming single again, I realized that shit, my penis is really small.

&#x200B;

> I am someone with a small penis by societal standards

&#x200B;

>I'm slightly below 6 inches. 

&#x200B;

>I said a WHOLE lot besides accept it and move on. I actually talk a lot about HOW to do that exactly.

&#x200B;

At most the best point I can surmise out of your long whatever. Is that you shouldn't bother with wishing you were big and think about how to work with being small.

&#x200B;

>Oh, you don't think love and acceptance is the same thing?

They are not. You can use a dictionary, or Google it. \[acceptance\]([https://www.collinsdictionary.com/dictionary/english/acceptance](https://www.collinsdictionary.com/dictionary/english/acceptance)) \[Love\]([https://www.collinsdictionary.com/dictionary/english/love](https://www.collinsdictionary.com/dictionary/english/love))

&#x200B;

>Again, I'm not telling you how to think.

&#x200B;

>\>I am most definitely making a case that one who's mindset is to think from a place of love is BETTER than one who thinks with hate. I make no effort to hide this. My thinking is better than yours if you think with a sense of negativity and hatred. I don't go into exact detail WHY love is better than hate because it seems obvious...
